# sltp-tg-bot

A production Telegram bot that bridges Telegram users to one or more MetaTrader 5
trading accounts running the **BulkSLTPUpdater** EA on Windows VPSes.

The Python service runs on a small Ubuntu droplet (e.g. DigitalOcean) and exposes:

* an **aiogram** Telegram bot for traders & admins, and
* a **FastAPI** bridge that each MT5 EA polls for jobs and reports alerts to.

Companion to MT5 EA `BulkSLTPUpdater` v1.3.0 (separate build).

## Author

* **Thanh Nguyen**
* Email: [thanhglobalist@gmail.com](mailto:thanhglobalist@gmail.com)
* Telegram: [@thanhglobalist](https://t.me/thanhglobalist)

## Languages

The bot ships with full translations for **three** languages and detects the
user's Telegram client language on first `/start` (override anytime via `/lang`):

* 🇬🇧 English (`en`)
* 🇯🇵 日本語 (`ja`)
* 🇻🇳 Tiếng Việt (`vi`)

## Highlights

* **Per-account permissions** — `view`, `view_close`, `full`, plus admin.
* **Tenant isolation enforced in SQL** — users can never see other tenants' data.
* **Stranger lockout** — non-members get only the localised "private bot" line.
* **Long-poll bridge** — EAs pull jobs over HTTPS; works through restrictive
  firewalls without exposing MT5 itself.
* **Push alerts** — position open/close, margin warnings, daily summary.
* **Hardened systemd unit + nginx + Docker artifacts** included.

## Quick start

```bash
git clone https://example.com/sltp-tg-bot.git
cd sltp-tg-bot
python3.11 -m venv venv && source venv/bin/activate
pip install -e ".[dev]"
cp .env.example .env       # fill in BOT_TOKEN and ADMIN_USER_ID
python scripts/init_db.py  # creates schema, prompts for admin user
python -m sltp_tg_bot.main
```

For full production deployment (systemd, nginx + Let's Encrypt, Docker,
backups, log rotation, on-call runbook) **see the DEVOPS guide** that ships
alongside this repo.

## Project layout

```
sltp-tg-bot/
├── pyproject.toml
├── .env.example
├── README.md
├── LICENSE
├── systemd/sltp-tg-bot.service
├── nginx/sltp-tg-bot.conf
├── docker/{Dockerfile,docker-compose.yml}
├── scripts/{init_db.py,backup_to_spaces.sh,rotate_token.py}
├── src/sltp_tg_bot/
│   ├── main.py            # entry — runs bot + bridge in one process
│   ├── config.py
│   ├── db.py
│   ├── i18n.py            # EN + JA + VI translations
│   ├── utils.py
│   ├── bot/               # aiogram handlers, keyboards, formatters
│   └── bridge/            # FastAPI EA-facing API
└── tests/{test_db,test_auth,test_jobs}.py
```

## Tests

```bash
pip install -e ".[dev]"
pytest -q
```

The test suite covers schema creation, account & permission CRUD, role-based
authorization, tenant isolation, the at-least-one-admin invariant, the job
lifecycle (enqueue / claim / complete / expire), and key parity across all
three languages in `i18n.py`.

